From: Mahendra Mali (Max) <max@maxnet.lan>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:20:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] kernel: sched/rcu: tighten timer slack and accelerate RCU callback drainage for embedded gateways

================================================================================
MAXNET High-Performance Kernel Engine & Hardware Architecture Optimization
Engineered & Developed by Mahendra Mali (Max) for MAXNET Router OS
Copyright (c) 2026 Mahendra Mali - Max. All Rights Reserved.
================================================================================

On embedded quad-core Cortex-A73 routing platforms:
1. init_task.timer_slack_ns defaults to 50us, adding latency jitter to epoll loops
   and network packet timers.
2. RCU callback batches are throttled to 10 callbacks per invocation (DEFAULT_RCU_BLIMIT),
   causing conntrack and SKB destruction to lag behind allocation rates under
   multi-gigabit loads and hoarding memory until qhimark (10,000) is reached.

This MAXNET patch:
- Lowers default timer slack to 10us for crisp real-time scheduling.
- Increases DEFAULT_RCU_BLIMIT to 64 and lowers DEFAULT_RCU_QHIMARK to 2,048,
  accelerating memory reclamation during high-rate packet traffic.

Signed-off-by: Mahendra Mali (Max) <max@maxnet.lan>
---
--- a/init/init_task.c
+++ b/init/init_task.c
@@ -143,7 +143,7 @@
 	.journal_info	= NULL,
 	INIT_CPU_TIMERS(init_task)
 	.pi_lock	= __RAW_SPIN_LOCK_UNLOCKED(init_task.pi_lock),
-	.timer_slack_ns = 50000, /* 50 usec default slack */
+	.timer_slack_ns = 10000, /* MAXNET: 10 usec default slack for network responsiveness */
 	.thread_pid	= &init_struct_pid,
 	.thread_node	= LIST_HEAD_INIT(init_signals.thread_head),
 #ifdef CONFIG_AUDIT
--- a/kernel/rcu/tree.c
+++ b/kernel/rcu/tree.c
@@ -412,11 +412,12 @@
 	return false;
 }
 
-#define DEFAULT_RCU_BLIMIT (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_RCU_STRICT_GRACE_PERIOD) ? 1000 : 10)
+#define DEFAULT_RCU_BLIMIT (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_RCU_STRICT_GRACE_PERIOD) ? 1000 : 64)
 				// Maximum callbacks per rcu_do_batch ...
 #define DEFAULT_MAX_RCU_BLIMIT 10000 // ... even during callback flood.
+/* MAXNET: 64 callbacks per batch and 2048 qhimark accelerates memory reclamation on 512MB RAM */
 static long blimit = DEFAULT_RCU_BLIMIT;
-#define DEFAULT_RCU_QHIMARK 10000 // If this many pending, ignore blimit.
+#define DEFAULT_RCU_QHIMARK 2048 // If this many pending, ignore blimit.
 static long qhimark = DEFAULT_RCU_QHIMARK;
 #define DEFAULT_RCU_QLOMARK 100   // Once only this many pending, use blimit.
 static long qlowmark = DEFAULT_RCU_QLOMARK;
